{
  "id": "semantic_tokens/modifiers/12_callable",
  "topic": "semantic_tokens",
  "subtopic": "modifiers",
  "title": "Callable variables",
  "summary": "A variable, parameter or field whose type can be called is `callable`",
  "prose": "Function pointers, pointers to member functions, lambdas and objects of a\nclass with an `operator()`, its own or a base's, all carry it, at their\ndeclaration and at every use.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "struct Adder {\n    int operator()(int left, int right) const;\n};\n\nstruct Counter : Adder {};\n\nint apply(int (*operation)(int, int), Adder adder, Counter counter, int value) {\n    auto twice = [](int x) { return x * 2; };\n    void (Adder::*member)() = nullptr;\n    return operation(value, value) + adder(value, value) + counter(value, 1) + twice(value);\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
